hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16086","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, he said, Bushayr ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Suwayd ibn al-Numan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at al-Sahba in the year of Khaybar, and when he prayed Asr, he called for foods, and nothing was brought but sawiq. He said, so we kneaded, meaning we ate of it. And when Maghrib came, he rinsed, and we rinsed with him."
